<title>USA: Harris signs deals to provide TV equipment.</title>
<headline>Harris signs deals to provide TV equipment.</headline>
<dateline>QUINCY, Ill. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harris Corp said Monday it entered agreements to provide analog and digital television transmitter equipment for 18 television stations that have a combined potential value of more than $15 million.</p>
<p>Under the agreements, Harris will provide equipment for 12 television stations owned by Silver King Broadcasting and six owned by Post-Newsweek Stations Inc, Harris said.</p>
<p>((-- Reuter Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787 ))</p>
